      {
        "id": "284bea52-d887-42cd-accb-7f92b5bbd033",
        "layout": "title-content",
        "background": {
          "type": "color",
          "value": "#0d0a1b",
          "opacity": 1
        },
        "notes": "To understand where we are, we must look at the foundations. From basic tokenization to massive Transformer models, the architecture of language models has fundamentally evolved.",
        "elements": [
          {
            "id": "9396c08d-9621-459b-90bc-2d791cd60fc3",
            "type": "heading",
            "x": 120,
            "y": 90,
            "width": 1680,
            "height": 90,
            "content": "Core Foundations of Modern NLP",
            "style": {
              "fontFamily": "Outfit",
              "fontSize": 48,
              "fontWeight": 700,
              "color": "#f8fafc",
              "textAlign": "left"
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "5e5e4211-c3af-4ada-9d8d-fe0133e008be",
            "type": "text",
            "x": 120,
            "y": 220,
            "width": 1680,
            "height": 720,
            "content": "Key milestones powering today's conversational systems\n\n• Tokenization and parsing convert raw text into structured numerical representations\n\n• Transformer architectures leverage self-attention to capture long-range contextual dependencies\n\n• Pre-training and fine-tuning paradigms drastically reduce the need for task-specific data",
            "style": {
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 28,
              "fontWeight": 400,
              "color": "#f8fafc",
              "lineHeight": 1.9
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "18316f16-3a41-4ac3-b329-087dc66c6b1a",
        "layout": "two-column",
        "background": {
          "type": "color",
          "value": "#0d0a1b",
          "opacity": 1
        },
        "notes": "Comparing traditional methods with modern generative models highlights the sheer leap in capability. We've moved from rigid rules to fluid, context-aware comprehension.",
        "elements": [
          {
            "id": "0b1833c1-1c88-4451-a470-fa26f0b95cc7",
            "type": "heading",
            "x": 120,
            "y": 90,
            "width": 1680,
            "height": 90,
            "content": "Traditional vs. Generative Models",
            "style": {
              "fontFamily": "Outfit",
              "fontSize": 48,
              "fontWeight": 700,
              "color": "#f8fafc",
              "textAlign": "left"
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "9696a976-d071-4745-b4a2-1c4824273dda",
            "type": "shape",
            "x": 120,
